[17.465412, "o", "In the knowledge graph, countries are represented using their two-letter ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 codes as string values.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[17.465463, "o", "> For example, Greece is represented as \"GR\".\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[17.466753, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[17.466823, "o", "The query should return: \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ```\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[17.466867, "o", "SELECT ?professorName (GROUP_CONCAT(DISTINCT ?country; separator=\", \") AS ?countries)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ``` \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
