[18.393138, "o", "Warning: running headless with --yolo / approval-mode=yolo and no sandbox. All tool calls (shell, write, edit) auto-execute at this process's privilege level. Configure tools.executionSandbox on Linux or a supported legacy sandbox via --sandbox / QWEN_SANDBOX, or set QWEN_CODE_SUPPRESS_YOLO_WARNING=1 to silence this notice.\r\n"]
[139.107104, "o", "The query is written to `/app/solution.sparql` and validated against the graph.\r\n\r\n**Approach**\r\n\r\n- **Full professors**: `uni:role` filtered to contain \"Professor\" but not \"Assistant\"/\"Associate\"/\"Adjunct\"/\"Visiting\" (this excludes `Athanasios_Voulodimos` and `Stefan_Mueller`).\r\n- **EU location**: `VALUES ?euCountry` lists the 27 member states as of 2025-08-16 (incl. `GR`, `PT`, `ES`, `FR`, `DE`); the department's `uni:belongsTo` → `uni:locatedInCountry` must match.\r\n- **Currently enrolled** (relative to 2025-08-16): enrollment date ≤ today and no graduation date, or graduation date > today (this drops Students 18–23, 25, 26 whose graduation already passed).\r\n- **>10 students**: a sub-select counts `DISTINCT` students over all courses with `uni:isTaughtIn` that department, with `HAVING (COUNT(DISTINCT ?student) > 10)`.\r\n- **`?countries`**: a separate `worksIn` → department → university → country path so the concat covers *all* departments the professor works in, not just the qualifying one.\r\n\r\n**Verification output** (rdflib, `python3-rdflib` installed via apt):\r\n\r\n```\r\nrows: 3\r\n{Aristotle Tympas, GR}\r\n{Orfeas Menis,   US, GR}\r\n{Pepe Attanasio, GR, PT}\r\n```\r\n\r\nDepartment counts backing the filter: `ComputerScience_NTUA` 12, `HistoryAndPhilosophy_NKUA` 12, `Engineering_Berkeley` 11 (US — correctly rejected), `Biology_MIT` 7, `Mathematics_Sorbonne` 6.\r\n\r\nOne note: rdflib.js (tried first) rejects `VALUES` and comment lines, but the file is standard SPARQL 1.1 and parses fine in rdflib/ARQ.\r\n"]
